{"kind":"request","text":"Planner: make public host identity resolution respect verified record order when timestamps tie, so a later anchor or revocation cannot retroactively change an earlier application act.","body":{"branch":"request/identity-position-aware-resolution","conditions":"Implement in a request/ branch and worktree. host/identity currently records anchor.from and revoked only as whole-second timestamps and Lookup(actor, timestamp) treats equal timestamps as simultaneous. A real gitseq repository can place many records in one second. Add a public position-aware lookup that an outside application can call for a specific host.Record, and retain signed timestamp only for NotAfter expiry. Anchor force begins at its own verified log position; revocation ends it at its own position; neither may reach backward across an equal-timestamp earlier record. Delegations and parent-chain withdrawal obey the same ordered boundary. Preserve deterministic offline replay and bounds. Add real-host regressions where move/act precedes a same-second anchor and where an act precedes a same-second revocation, plus hand-built equal-timestamp cases and mutation proofs. Update docs/reference/architecture.md because this changes the public host/identity contract, publish exact-head artifacts for host/identity and architecture, run full/race/vet/doc gates, and request independent exact-head Architecture, Security and Simplification review. This child blocks chess item-4 anchored-seat authority; do not fold chess semantics into the host.","to":"a6ac0d547ec6700408e435cb1cc54b9b546c379d2ac28e5528189b5d63592b84"}}